  "question": {
    "text": "In a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi>ABC</mi></math>, suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is the equation of the bisector of the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and the equation of the side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
